# Local-dev vars for `wrangler dev`. Copy to .dev.vars and fill in the one blank below.
#
#   cp .dev.vars.example .dev.vars
#
# Never commit .dev.vars. In production set secrets with `wrangler secret put <NAME>`
# instead; plain vars go in wrangler.jsonc.
#
# SECURITY: ZOOCLAW_API_KEY authenticates this Worker as your whole organization. It must
# never reach the browser, a log, or a client bundle.

# ── The only thing you have to fill in ───────────────────────────────────────
# Your org API key (`zct_…`), issued from the org admin surface. The plaintext is shown
# exactly once when it is created.
ZOOCLAW_API_KEY=

# ── Local identity ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Stands in for Cloudflare Access so you are signed in locally. Any string works; it is
# the key your chats are stored under. Never set this in production - without it, and
# without Access configured, every request is rejected, which is the behaviour you want.
DEV_EMAIL=you@example.com

# ── Everything below is optional ─────────────────────────────────────────────

# Point at a different deployment. Unset, the SDK uses the public gateway.
# ZOOCLAW_API_URL=

# FIXED-AGENT MODE: use ONE pre-built agent (agt_…) for everyone and provision nothing.
# Demo/single-tenant only - each conversation still gets its own session, but everyone
# shares one agent's configuration. Unset it to exercise real per-user provisioning,
# which works out of the box in gateway mode.
# ZOOCLAW_AGENT_ID=

# Pin a sandbox Environment version at agent create. Unset, the system default is used.
# ZOOCLAW_ENVIRONMENT_ID=

# Shared gate key for embedding. When set, every /api/app/* call must present it
# (X-Embed-Key header or ?k= query) or gets 401.
# EMBED_KEY=
